  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-109662",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$  then \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}-{X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nHowever, in this case, we don't know whether ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent. Therefore, we do not have enough information to determine the answer.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
